## Implemented Contract

Selection:

- One backend-neutral seven-state value: none plus Node, exact Primitive
  occurrence, Mesh, Material, Camera, and Light.
- Primitive identity includes scene, node, primitive, and instance ordinal.
- Viewport selection/toggle requires a current immutable occurrence lookup
  bound to document revision, scene activation epoch, and mapping generation.
- Unknown ordinal, stale lookup, foreign authority, reused generation, and
  effective-hidden occurrence fail closed without selection effect.
- Explicit remaps bind source/target authority, document revision, scene epoch,
  and occurrence generation. Stale replay is a no-effect; ambiguous matching
  evidence clears rather than guessing by vector index.
- Accepted changes enqueue one ordered frame-end event and increment one
  selection revision. Identical set and empty clear are idempotent. Event
  allocation completes before the no-throw state commit.
- Same-value identity remap or refreshed occurrence publication updates
  internal fences without emitting a selection event.
- Browser focus requests reveal and scroll with `selectTab=false`.

Clipboard:

- Copy emits exact ASCII `gltf_material:<unsigned decimal>` resolved against
  the current document at copy time.
- Parsing consumes the complete suffix, accepts leading zero input, rejects
  signs, whitespace, junk, decimal points, non-ASCII digits, and checked
  `uint64` overflow.
- Canonical out-of-range input remains enabled but invalid and non-applicable.
- Paste availability is resolved again from the OS clipboard and active
  document on every click. No stable Material ID survives a document switch.
- The codec has no history mutation or ImGui/RHI dependency.

Viewport metrics:

- Immutable logical half-open viewport, framebuffer logical origin,
  non-uniform framebuffer scale, explicit color/depth physical rectangles,
  color/depth attachment extents, viewport generation, projection/view
  identities, and clip convention.
- Color physical coordinates are the exact floor/ceil result of one DPI
  conversion. Arbitrary full-attachment substitution is rejected.
- Unequal color/depth targets use an explicit normalized depth rectangle and
  `logicalToDepthPhysical()` mapping.
- All eight D4 surface transforms have closed mapping semantics for color and
  depth targets; unknown transforms fail closed.
- Perspective and orthographic constant-logical-pixel scaling require finite
  positive view depth and preserve logical size across DPI changes.
- Public headers contain no ImGui, GLFW, renderer, RHI, native backend, dense
  draw index, mutable document pointer, or forbidden reference helper type.

